# 1. Executive summary

Family 1 should introduce a scoped public/auth design system without changing backend contracts or Families 2–6 product surfaces. Preserve server sessions, current CSRF transport, existing route compatibility, and Family 3’s merchant `/` workspace ownership.

# 2. Repository areas inspected

- `frontend/src/App.tsx`, `api.ts`, `state/AuthContext.tsx`, `sessionEvents.ts`
- Current Family 1 pages, `Layout`, `Navbar`, `Footer`, `SessionTimeoutManager`, global CSS
- Family 2–6 routes, shells, styles, tests, and business workspace README
- `AuthController`, `UserController`, `SessionController`, `BusinessApiController`
- Auth/OTP/LINE/business services, DTOs, exception handler, Security config, application config, tests

# 3. Repository differences from approved Redesign Contract

- Login backend accepts `username` and `password` only; current UI incorrectly says “使用者名稱 / 電子郵件”.
- Current login uses response data directly; it does not call `AuthContext.refresh()` before navigation.
- Current `safeInternalReturnTo` only checks `/` and rejects `//`; it permits auth loops and role-incompatible paths.
- Current customer default after login is `/`.
- `/` renders Family 3 merchant workspace for authenticated merchants.
- Merchant registration creates `BusinessData` immediately; `/business/setup` is primarily for merchant LINE-first accounts lacking business data.
- Force-change UI incorrectly has confirmation input; backend accepts exactly `newPassword`.
- OTP identifier is currently exposed in `?account=`.
- OTP resend has no separate endpoint; resend is the OTP request endpoint.
- Customer/merchant registration duplicate errors are returned as HTTP `400`, although global duplicate handling uses `409` elsewhere.
- Current auth pages use global product `Layout`, Bootstrap navbar/footer, and card styling.
- Existing `sessionStorage` business draft includes plaintext password.
- Authenticated users are not redirected away from login/registration/recovery routes.
- `/business/setup` currently redirects completed merchants to `/business/info`; this is a Family 4-owned destination.
- Wildcard currently redirects to `/`.

