# 12. Credential-login backend contract

| Item | Contract |
|---|---|
| Method/path | `POST /api/auth/login` |
| Auth | Public |
| CSRF | Ignored by backend; current client may still attach token |
| Body | `{ username, password }` |
| Success | `200 { success: true, message, data: UserResponse }` |
| Failure | `401 { success:false, message:"帳號或密碼錯誤" }`; `429` rate limit; generic `500` |
| Session | Creates and saves Spring Security HTTP session |
| Rate limits | IP 20/minute; account 10/minute |
| Redirect | Frontend only |

# 13. Login UI/interaction contract

- Fields: username, password; do not claim email login.
- `autocomplete="username"` and `current-password`.
- Shared `PasswordField`, visible toggle, pending-disabled submit.
- Preserve username after recoverable failure; clear password after every credential submission result.
- Inline normalized error only; no raw API messages.
- Login resolves destination only after authoritative refresh.
- CTA: `登入`; booking return context only if valid `returnTo` exists.

# 14. Login return-context contract

- Display booking context only for safe customer-compatible return paths such as `/reservation/new` or `/my/reservations`.
- Store only sanitized path plus query under a dedicated short-lived session key.
- Consume once when navigation succeeds.
- Do not display raw URLs, business routes, external URLs, OTP/account identifiers, or untrusted query content.
- Generic login has no return-context block.

# 15. Generic-login contract

