# 34. Safe returnTo contract

`safeInternalReturnTo(source)` must:

- Accept only non-empty internal paths beginning with exactly one `/`.
- Reject protocol URLs, `//`, backslashes, control characters, malformed URI text, and paths that fail URL parsing.
- Preserve valid query strings.
- Reject auth-loop routes: `/login`, `/register`, `/register-business`, `/forgot-password`, `/forgot-password/verify`, `/force-change-password`.
- Normalize to pathname plus search; drop fragments.
- Validate role compatibility after syntax validation.
- Persist only sanitized value; consume only after successful destination resolution.
- Never use `window.location` with untrusted redirect data.

# 35. Role-compatible destination contract

| Destination family | Customer | Merchant |
|---|---:|---:|
| `/reservation/new`, `/my/reservations` | Yes | No |
| `/preferred-businesses`, `/profile`, customer notification settings | Verify existing guard; default allow only current customer-supported routes | No unless existing route explicitly supports merchant |
| Merchant workspace/reservation management/service/settings | No | Yes, business required |
| `/business/setup` | No | Yes, no business only |
| Auth/recovery routes | No as return target | No as return target |

Unknown paths are rejected rather than treated as safe merely because they are internal.

